# Build output and the packaged release payloads. `dist/` is what the build step
# uploads (and what the smoke gate assembles from); `release/` is what
# scripts/release-artifacts.sh writes (a ~20 MB tarball that embeds a CPython).
# Neither is source, and an un-ignored `release/` is one `git add -A` away from
# committing a 20 MB binary to history.
#
# genproj's template does not carry these (regenerated 2026-09-20), so this
# block has to be re-applied after every regeneration —
# docs/genproj-target-gap.md §7, trap 5.
dist/
release/



